# feat: chunk and retry UAL queries, flag data gaps

## Summary

Large Unified Audit Log pulls (wide date ranges, `-AllUsers`, the 180-day
sign-in/risky-operation profiles) can fail partway through when Exchange
times out, throttles, or drops the session — and until now those failures
were easy to miss, leaving a quietly incomplete dataset.

This brings `Get-IRTUnifiedAuditLog` in line with the resilience work
already done in `Get-IRTEntraSignInLog`, and goes one step further: when a
query can't be recovered, the gap is written into the data itself so it's
impossible to overlook in the exported workbook.

## What changed

**`Get-IRTUnifiedAuditLog`**

- **`-ChunkDays`** is now a real parameter (default 182) instead of a
  hardcoded value, so you can shrink the per-request window when a pull
  keeps timing out.
- **Per-chunk token refresh** — a long multi-chunk run no longer outlives
  the token's refresh window and starts failing with auth errors.
- **`-ChunkDelaySeconds`** (default 2) adds a small pause between chunks to
  stay under Exchange throttling limits.
- **`-ThrottleDelaySeconds`** (default 60) drives retry-with-backoff around
  every `Search-UnifiedAuditLog` call. Because Exchange reports transient
  failures with inconsistent error text, this retries on *any* terminal
  error rather than pattern-matching messages, refreshes the token between
  attempts, and records the full exception to the PSFramework debug log for
  later troubleshooting.
- **Visible "DATA MISSING" marker** — if a query still fails after all
  retries, the function raises an error *and* inserts a marker row into the
  results rather than silently returning partial data. The marker is shaped
  like a real UAL record so it flows through dedup, sorting, and the sheet
  builders; it sorts to the failed time window, shouts in the UserIds and
  Operation columns, and carries the failed query, window, and exception in
  its Raw column. The run continues so the rest of the data is still
  collected around the gap.

**`Show-IRTUnifiedAuditLog`**

- Data-gap markers always bypass operation-based sheet filtering, so a gap
  shows up on every sheet — including the SignInLogs profile, which is
  exactly the kind of long pull prone to these failures.

## Behavior notes

- A failed query no longer aborts the whole run; you get the maximum data
  available plus a flagged gap. (If a hard stop is ever preferred, it's a
  one-line change in the catch blocks.)
- If *every* query fails, the workbook now contains only marker rows, which
  makes a total failure obvious too, rather than a bare "0 logs" message.

## Testing

- Offline Pester suite for the function passes (10/10), including two new
  tests covering the retry count and the marker passthrough to
  `Show-IRTUnifiedAuditLog`.
- Formatting and PSSA checks (ModuleSyntax, LineLength, FormatOperator,
  JoinPath, NonASCII, BacktickContinuation, WriteVerboseDebug, PSSA) are
  clean on all three changed files.
- Online tests were not run (they require a live Microsoft 365 session).

